<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constitutionalist Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1913">1913</a>–<a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Constitutionalist Army was the force raised in 1913 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venustiano-carranza">Venustiano Carranza</a>, governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coahuila">Coahuila</a>, to restore constitutional government after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victoriano-huerta">Victoriano Huerta</a>'s coup. Under commanders such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alvaro-obregon">Álvaro Obregón</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pancho-villa">Pancho Villa</a> it defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huerta">Huerta</a> in 1914, and after the split with Villa and Zapata it won the civil war of 1915. It became the core of the post-revolutionary federal army.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constitutionalist-army.jpg" alt="Constitutionalist Army" width="297" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gustavo Casasola · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caballer%C3%ADa_constitucionalista.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
